.TH SDL_SetTrayEntryCallback 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetTrayEntryCallback \- Sets a callback to be invoked when the entry is selected.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_SetTrayEntryCallback(SDL_TrayEntry *entry, SDL_TrayCallback callback, void *userdata);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I entry
the entry to be updated\[char46]
.TP
.I callback
a callback to be invoked when the entry is selected\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
an optional pointer to pass extra data to the callback when it will be invoked\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called on the thread that created the tray\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

